SUMMARY:Glotech Cantata: A Performance of Images
LOCATION:Brattleboro Museum & Art Center\, 10 Vernon St\, Brattleboro\, VT 
 05301
DESCRIPTION:Glotech Cantata is an afternoon of movement\, sound\, and still
  images that interprets the dance between women and influencer marketing. 
 Taking the Glotech LED facial mask as its motif\, the work meditates upon 
 our era of aspirational social media\, where women are both the authors an
 d the objects of images. This site-responsive performance uses “painting
 s”—large printed panels of still lifes\, masks\, and color abstraction
 s—as both props and a movable set that frame\, conceal\, and cast color 
 onto dancers\, who pit improvised movements against stylized gestures and 
 words.\nhttps://www.brattleboromuseum.org/event/glotech-cantata-a-performa
 nce-of-images/\nFrom Pushpin Western Mass: https://pushpin.city/westernma/
URL:https://www.brattleboromuseum.org/event/glotech-cantata-a-performance-o
 f-images/
END:VEVENT
